.TH REDHAT-AI-CONFIGURATOR 1 "October 2026" "redhat-ai-configurator 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redhat-ai-configurator \- configure goose for Red Hat AI MaaS (rhai-maas) and EnMaaS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redhat-ai-configurator
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B redhat-ai-configurator
configures the
.BR goose (1)
AI agent with the user's own Red Hat AI MaaS and EnMaaS API keys.
Run it without arguments for the interactive terminal installer.
.PP
The tool validates each key against the service before writing anything,
merges its settings into the existing goose configuration, and backs up every
file it replaces. It never creates API keys: you create them in the browser.
.PP
Service endpoints are configured rather than embedded. Set them in
\fI/etc/redhat-ai-configurator/endpoints.conf\fR or through the environment
variables listed below. A fresh install uses placeholder example.com values and
warns until they are replaced.
.PP
Red Hat AI MaaS needs the corporate VPN to be
.BR off ;
EnMaaS needs it
.BR on .
The installer shows which is required at each step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Run without prompts. Implied by \fB--yes\fR, \fB--dry-run\fR and a non-TTY.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Accept defaults without prompting.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " ID"
Providers to configure, comma separated: \fBrhai-maas\fR, \fBenmaas\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-key-file " PATH"
Read \fINAME=value\fR lines from PATH, or \fB-\fR for stdin. The file must be
mode 0600 and owned by the invoking user. Recognised names are
\fBRHAI_MAAS_API_KEY\fR and \fBENMAAS_API_KEY\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keep-existing
Reuse a key that is already stored instead of requiring it again.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " PROVIDER=MODEL"
Set the default model, for example \fBenmaas=rits/zai-org/glm-5-3\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " MODE"
goose tool mode: \fBauto\fR, \fBapprove\fR, \fBsmart_approve\fR or \fBchat\fR.
The default is \fBapprove\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keyring
Store keys in the system keyring instead of \fBsecrets.yaml\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no-validate
Do not call the services to check keys. Useful for offline image builds.
.TP
.B \-\-require-validation
Fail when a key could not be validated, for example on the wrong VPN.
.TP
.B \-\-no-verify
Do not run \fBgoose info --check\fR afterwards.
.TP
.B \-\-rollback-on-failure
Restore the previous configuration if verification fails.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print what would change and exit without writing.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|json"
Output format. JSON is intended for automation.
.TP
.BI \-\-config-dir " DIR"
goose configuration directory. Default: \fB~/.config/goose\fR, or
\fB$GOOSE_PATH_ROOT/config\fR when that variable is set.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check the current configuration without changing it.
.TP
.B \-\-list-models
Print the models the service offers, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-root
Permit running as root. Containers and image builds only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RHAI_MAAS_API_KEY
Red Hat AI MaaS API key.
.TP
.B ENMAAS_API_KEY
EnMaaS API key.
.TP
.B RHAI_MAAS_BASE_URL
OpenAI-compatible base URL, including \fB/v1\fR.
.TP
.B ENMAAS_BASE_URL
Anthropic-compatible root, without \fB/v1\fR (goose appends \fBv1/messages\fR).
.TP
.BR RHAI_MAAS_KEY_PAGE ", " RHAI_MAAS_HELP_URL
Page for creating a key, and the help link shown in the UI.
.TP
.BR ENMAAS_KEY_PAGE ", " ENMAAS_HELP_URL
Page for creating a key, and the help link shown in the UI.
.TP
.BR ENMAAS_ELIGIBILITY_URL ", " ENMAAS_SLACK
Optional access-request page and help channel.
.TP
.B GOOSE_PATH_ROOT
Relocates goose's configuration directory; useful in tests.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a successful dry run.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: bad flag, no provider, or no TTY without \fB--non-interactive\fR.
.TP
.B 3
goose is missing or older than 1.38.
.TP
.B 4
A key is missing, unreadable, or was rejected.
.TP
.B 5
A service is unreachable (network or VPN).
.TP
.B 6
A configuration file could not be written.
.TP
.B 7
The configuration was written but \fBgoose info --check\fR failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/redhat-ai-configurator/endpoints.conf
Service endpoints. Environment variables take precedence.
.TP
.I ~/.config/goose/config.yaml
Provider, model and mode. Merged, backed up before writing.
.TP
.I ~/.config/goose/custom_providers/*.json
Declarative provider definitions for rhai-maas, enmaas and enmaas-openai.
.TP
.I ~/.config/goose/secrets.yaml
API keys, mode 0600, when file storage is selected.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure both providers from environment variables:
.PP
.nf
export RHAI_MAAS_API_KEY=...
export ENMAAS_API_KEY=...
redhat-ai-configurator --non-interactive --provider rhai-maas,enmaas
.fi
.PP
Read keys from stdin and emit machine-readable output:
.PP
.nf
printf 'RHAI_MAAS_API_KEY=%s\\n' "$KEY" |
  redhat-ai-configurator --non-interactive --provider rhai-maas \\
  --key-file - --format json
.fi
.SH NOTES
Run the tool as the user who will use goose, not as root. Keys are created by
the user in the browser; the tool only validates and stores them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR goose (1)
